# CODEOWNERS
#
# Review requests route to the owner of the path that changed. GitHub only offers
# a collaborator as a reviewer once their handle appears here, so adding a
# teammate to this file is part of the add-a-teammate procedure in
# ../CONTRIBUTING.md — the other two steps are the collaborator invitation and
# the citation entry in ../CITATION.cff.
#
# At bootstrap the repository has exactly one contributor, so every path is
# owned by @andrewhmir. Add a teammate by appending their handle to the default
# line and to the lane lines they own, for example:
#
#     *       @andrewhmir @teammate
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the specific lines below must stay after
# the default. Keeping one line per lane means a lane owner can be added without
# granting review rights over the whole repository.

# Default: anything not matched by a more specific line below.
*           @andrewhmir

# Lanes
/firmware/  @andrewhmir
/notebooks/ @andrewhmir
/webapp/    @andrewhmir
/data/      @andrewhmir

# Cross-cutting paths, which are not a fourth lane.
/docs/      @andrewhmir
/specs/     @andrewhmir
/tests/     @andrewhmir

# Repository platform configuration: workflow, templates, Dependabot, CODEOWNERS.
/.github/   @andrewhmir
